First contentful paint in a WebView without a compositor: no NULL LayerTreeHost dereference.

WebFrameWidgetImpl::NotifyVizFMPSwap() (neva, USE_NEVA_APPRUNTIME) queues a swap promise on
widget_base_->LayerTreeHost() without a check. A WebView that does not composite has no LayerTreeHost, and its
first contentful paint crashed the renderer: SIGSEGV at 0x1ec in cc::SwapPromiseManager::QueueSwapPromise, from
PaintTiming::SetFirstContentfulPaint -> ChromeClientImpl::NotifyVizFMPSwap. adblock-tester.com crashed the tab
this way ("Aw, Snap!", error 11) on the LG C1, in WebOS-Chromium 0.0.66 and in our build. Every other
LayerTreeHost user in web_frame_widget_impl.cc returns early on !View()->does_composite(). This one does the same.

diff -ru a/src/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/web_frame_widget_impl.cc b/src/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/web_frame_widget_impl.cc
--- a/src/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/web_frame_widget_impl.cc	2026-11-18 21:00:00
+++ b/src/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/web_frame_widget_impl.cc	2026-11-18 21:00:00
@@ -4031,6 +4031,10 @@

 void WebFrameWidgetImpl::NotifyVizFMPSwap(bool is_first_contentful_paint,
                                           bool did_reset_container_state) {
+  // A WebView that does not composite has no LayerTreeHost (the same guard as
+  // the other LayerTreeHost users in this file).
+  if (!View()->does_composite() || !widget_base_->LayerTreeHost())
+    return;
   widget_base_->LayerTreeHost()->QueueSwapPromise(
       std::make_unique<VizFMPPromise>(is_first_contentful_paint,
                                       did_reset_container_state));
